WEBVTT

00:00:10.328 --> 00:00:11.448
Stop! Hey!

00:00:11.528 --> 00:00:12.568
(GIGGLES)

00:00:12.648 --> 00:00:14.168
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:29.808
(BLEEPING)

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:32.408
-Oh, you've got to be joking.
-What's the problem?

00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:34.288
-He's in the loo.
-So, go in!

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:37.048
-I can't go into the men's loo!
-Time is of the essence.

00:00:37.168 --> 00:00:39.168
All right.

00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:50.568
Oh! Whatever you do,
I would not go in there!

00:00:52.168 --> 00:00:54.768
Hey! A Gremlin and a Pacer!

00:00:54.848 --> 00:00:56.408
No offense to your makes and models,

00:00:56.528 --> 00:00:59.168
but you break down harder
than my cousin Betsy

00:00:59.248 --> 00:01:01.168
after she got left at the altar!

00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:03.528
What the...? Whoa. Are you OK?

00:01:03.608 --> 00:01:05.688
-I'm fine.
-Hey! Tow truck!

00:01:05.768 --> 00:01:09.248
We'd like to get to our private business
here, if you don't mind.

00:01:09.328 --> 00:01:10.808
Oh, yeah, sorry.

00:01:10.848 --> 00:01:13.408
Don't let me get in the way
of your private business.

00:01:13.488 --> 00:01:17.248
Oh, a little advice. When you hear
a giggle and see that waterfall,

00:01:17.328 --> 00:01:19.208
you best press that green button.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:21.448
-Thank you.
-It's to adjust the temperature.

00:01:21.528 --> 00:01:24.128
-Got it.
-And it's in Celsius, not Fahrenheit.

00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:25.648
BOTH: Get out of here!

00:01:25.688 --> 00:01:29.848
All right, then. And when she starts
gigglin', prepare to be squirted.

00:01:30.728 --> 00:01:32.568
'Scuse me, ma'am. (BACKFIRES)

00:01:32.688 --> 00:01:34.608
Dad-gum pistachio ice cream.

00:01:34.688 --> 00:01:38.288
-This cannot be him.
-FINN: Is he American?

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:40.728
Look out, ladies.
Mater's fittin' to get funky.

00:01:40.848 --> 00:01:43.208
-Extremely.
-Then it's him.

00:01:43.808 --> 00:01:45.288
-Hello.
-Well, hello.

00:01:45.408 --> 00:01:48.048
A Volkswagen Karmann Ghia
has no radiator.

00:01:48.168 --> 00:01:50.728
Well, of course it doesn't.
That's 'cause it's air-cooled.

00:01:50.848 --> 00:01:53.608
Perfect.
Erm...I'm from the Tokyo Station.

00:01:53.688 --> 00:01:56.408
'Course, Karmann Ghias
weren't the only ones.

00:01:56.488 --> 00:02:00.288
Besides the Beetles, you had Type 3
Squarebacks with the Pancake motors.

00:02:00.368 --> 00:02:02.688
-Yeah, OK. I get it.
-And before both of them

00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:04.488
there's the Type 2 buses.

00:02:04.568 --> 00:02:06.728
-My buddy Fillmore's one of them.
-Listen!

00:02:06.848 --> 00:02:08.568
Erm... We should find somewhere
more private.

00:02:09.488 --> 00:02:11.408
Gee, don't you think that's a little...?

00:02:11.488 --> 00:02:14.568
You're right. Impossible to know
which areas here are compromised.

00:02:14.688 --> 00:02:16.888
-So, when can I see you again?
-Well, let's see.

00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:19.768
-Tomorrow I'll be out there at the races.
-Got it.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.248
We'll rendezvous then.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.168
-There you are. Where have you been?
-What's a "rendezvous"?

00:02:25.288 --> 00:02:27.088
-Er... It's like a date.
-A date?

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:28.608
Mater, what's going on?

00:02:28.688 --> 00:02:31.448
What's going on is
I got me a date tomorrow.

00:02:31.528 --> 00:02:33.448
-(SPEAKS ITALIAN)
-Guido don't believe you.

00:02:33.528 --> 00:02:36.608
Believe it.
My new girlfriend just said so.

00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:39.688
Hey, there she is. Hey! Hey, lady!

00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:41.648
See you tomorrow!

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.208
-(SPEAKS ITALIAN)
-Guido still don't believe you.

00:02:46.288 --> 00:02:50.128
-I got to admit, you tricked us real good.
-And we don't like being tricked.

00:02:50.208 --> 00:02:52.088
-(CHUCKLES)
-ACER: What's so funny?

00:02:52.128 --> 00:02:56.288
Well, I was just wearing a disguise.
You guys are stuck looking like that.

00:02:58.808 --> 00:03:02.408
Allinol? Thanks, fellas.
I hear this stuff is good for you.

00:03:02.488 --> 00:03:04.288
So you think.

00:03:04.328 --> 00:03:06.888
Allinol by itself is good for you.

00:03:07.608 --> 00:03:09.368
(WHIRRING)

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:13.328
But after microscopic examination

00:03:13.408 --> 00:03:16.088
I have found
that it has one small weakness.

00:03:16.168 --> 00:03:18.968
When hit with
an electromagnetic pulse,

00:03:19.088 --> 00:03:22.128
it becomes extremely dangerous.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.008
Smile for the camera.

00:03:24.168 --> 00:03:26.168
Is that all you want? I got a whole act.

00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:29.768
You were very interested in this camera
on the oil platform.

00:03:29.848 --> 00:03:33.848
Now, you will witness
what it really does.

00:03:33.928 --> 00:03:37.528
-Whatever you say, Professor.
-You talked up a lot of cars last night.

00:03:37.648 --> 00:03:39.848
-Which one's your associate?
-Your mother.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:43.528
Oh, no, I'm sorry, it was your sister.
I can't tell them apart these days.

00:03:43.608 --> 00:03:45.368
Could I start it now, Professor Z?

00:03:45.488 --> 00:03:47.528
ZÜNDAPP: Go 50% power.

00:03:47.608 --> 00:03:48.648
(WHIRRING)

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:53.448
This camera is actually
an electromagnetic pulse emitter.

00:03:53.528 --> 00:03:55.488
What about her? Did you give it to her?

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:58.848
The allinol is now heating to a boil,

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:03.848
dramatically expanding, causing the
engine block to crack under the stress,

00:04:03.928 --> 00:04:06.408
forcing oil
into the combustion chamber.

00:04:06.488 --> 00:04:08.368
How about him? Did you talk to him?

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:12.048
What do I care?
I can replace an engine block.

00:04:12.208 --> 00:04:15.488
You may be able to,
but after full impact of the pulse...

00:04:15.568 --> 00:04:19.048
unfortunately...
there will be nothing to replace.

00:04:19.728 --> 00:04:22.208
ACER: How about him?
Does he have it?

00:04:26.208 --> 00:04:28.208
That's him. He's the one.

00:04:28.688 --> 00:04:30.568
-Roger that, Professor Z.
-No!

00:04:30.648 --> 00:04:31.728
Yes, sir.

00:04:31.808 --> 00:04:35.728
We believe the infiltrator has passed
along sensitive information.

00:04:36.168 --> 00:04:39.008
I will take care of it
before any damage can be done.

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:42.088
The project is still on schedule.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:45.648
You will find the second agent
and kill him.

00:04:46.768 --> 00:04:48.768
(WHIRRING)

